A||||7||falconhulk||Aftermarket glovebox||||1||
Z||000000||falconhulk||08-28-2001||11:49 AM||||How are these things attached?  Do you have to cut out the map pocket?  If so how does the material respond to that?  Does it look right?  Does the glove box screw into the plastic behind the dash?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/i-4_b_l.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||08-28-2001||12:54 PM||||The map pocket is held in by 4 nuts behind the dash 3 of which can actually be reached. I just snapped off the 4th one. The glove box comes with 4 screws and just screws into the recess where the map pocket was. Very easy installation.||||reg||1
Z||000002||jch82||08-28-2001||12:55 PM||||The factory map pocket is held on with 6 speed nuts. You have to take the dash out to get to them. I would assume that the aftermarket glovebox is held in with the same 6 nuts.<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||mbramble||08-28-2001||12:57 PM||||You need to pull the dash so that you can get at the four tin nuts that hold the map pocket to the dash.  Then you install the aftermarket dash in its place using the same mounting holes.  Reinstall the dash.||||reg||1
Z||000004||falconhulk||08-28-2001||01:22 PM||||heh heh 2 for removing the dash and one against!  Which is it?  Phil, the nuts are metal or plastic?  Is it 6 or 4?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Bill Osmer||08-28-2001||01:32 PM||||Depends whether you're trying to save the map pocket for future use or not. I chose to snap the screws off - was way easier than removing the dash (and there are many spare map pockets out in the boneyards). The "new" glovebox mounts with _4_ sheet metal screwsin new locations from the stock holes. When I was finished, over a year ago), the new glovebox was (and is) very secure to the dash. Looks like it should have been thenre from the factory. The only bad thing is the "cup holders" aren't very good at being cup holders. <P>------------------<BR>Bill Osmer<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcardsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000006||KissMySSFiero||08-28-2001||02:21 PM||||on  my map pocket i have 4 speed nuts.  its a thin nut that can be pushed on rather than spun on, but has to be spun off.  they go on a plastic stud.  which can be broken fairly easily if you dont wnat to save the map pocket.  i dont knwo how the glovebox mounts so i wouldnt know what to tell ya there.<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||08-28-2001||02:55 PM||||4 stamped tin nuts, plastic nubs on back. I just snapped them all off to put new map pocket in Lisas. just glued new one in place. old one was still fine, just needed to be glued in too. (she changed from tan to gray btw)||||reg||1
